# Everything here is OPTIONAL. With an empty file the app reads Spotify's public
# pages and writes to Deezer through a browser login - no registrations at all.

# --- Spotify (optional) --------------------------------------------------
# Adds exact ISRC matching and lifts the 100-track ceiling of the public pages.
# https://developer.spotify.com/dashboard -> Create app. Any redirect URI will do.
SPOTIFY_CLIENT_ID=
SPOTIFY_CLIENT_SECRET=

# --- Deezer (optional) ---------------------------------------------------
# A registered app is the documented, stable way to write playlists.
# https://developers.deezer.com/myapps -> Create a new application
#   Application domain : localhost
#   Redirect URL       : http://localhost:4870/api/deezer/callback
DEEZER_APP_ID=
DEEZER_APP_SECRET=

# --- Deezer without an app (optional) ------------------------------------
# The same cookie the app asks for on its own page; setting it here just means you
# do not have to paste it in the UI. From a logged-in deezer.com: DevTools ->
# Application -> Cookies -> arl. Treat it like a password - it IS your Deezer
# session. Pasting it in the UI stores it in data/gw.json instead.
DEEZER_ARL=

PORT=4870
